  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of international visits held to foster cooperation, learn best practices, and prevent corruption. 
2. Number of risk assessments conducted to identify corruption prone areas in various service delivery sectors &#x2013; health, education, construction, electricity etc. 
3. Number of government officials with enhanced capacity to integrate anti-corruption measures
4. Number of analytical documents, policy papers and opinion polls produced for policy fine &#x2013; tuning and inform reform initiatives</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2016">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Nil study visits took place to learn international best practices, and foster cooperation 
2. Lack of corruption risks assessments in place to identify entry points aimed at improving delivery of public services 
3. Government officials lack skills and knowledge to integrate anti-corruption measures across the state sector
4. Absence of strong evidence based analytical documents, policy papers and opinion polls to implement sustainable reform initiatives</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Newly - established AC Agency of Uzbekistan is supported and guided in the formulation of the legal and institutional framework 
2. Hold up to 10 webinars and/or online discussion meetings on compliance, code of conduct, anticorruption reforms and best practices</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 4 laws and decrees reviewed and scrutinized to strengthen the institutional framework of the Uzbekistan&#x2019;s AC Agency.
2. 11 webinars on issues pertaining to corruption prevention, integrity, transparency, compliance, and international practices are organized</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Enhance the capacity of the AC Agency of Uzbekistan to produce solid analytical documents and implement sustainable policy reforms 
2. Provide support to the AC Agency of Uzbekistan in reviewing and producing corruption prevention mechanisms, analytical papers, and policy memos
3. Produce analytical document on nexus between corruption and contemporary forms of slavery in partnership with the Principality of Liechtenstein</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The capacity of the AC Agency is further enhanced to develop policy and regulatory acts aimed at sustaining reform initiatives, including those on human rights and gender
2. Visionary guidance provided to the Government of Uzbekistan and the AC Agency in reviewing and producing 24 laws, bylaws, strategies, and action plans to bolster national anti-corruption efforts 
3. One study exploring linkages between corruption and contemporary forms of slavery is produced and presented to government officials, development partners, CSOs and other key stakeholders at the global fora</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.At least 50 practitioners from Uzbekistan enhanced their capacity to integrate anti-corruption measures and solutions in service delivery 
2.At least 3 draft legations/laws/decrees have received policy and advisory support from ACPIS and IRH</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.410 practitioners (315 male and 95 females) from Uzbekistan enhanced their capacity to integrate anti-corruption measures and solutions in service delivery
2.5 draft legations/laws/decrees have received policy and advisory support from ACPIS and IRH</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
